[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]
[b]MO2 Revamped[/b] is an unofficial community edition of [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer]Mod Organizer 2[/url] v2.5.2 (USVFS 0.5.7.2), built for Elden Ring. It keeps the MO2 workflow you know (virtual file system, profiles, plugin and mod lists) and adds a refreshed interface, dedicated Elden Ring tools and a guided installer.

[b]This project is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, the Mod Organizer 2 team, Nexus Mods, FromSoftware or Bandai Namco.[/b] All upstream names, copyrights and licenses are preserved.

[b]Play offline.[/b] Mods are for offline play only. To avoid the online connection notices, set [b]System > Network > Launch Setting[/b] to [b]Play Offline[/b] in the game.

[b]Verify the download[/b]
The installer is [b]not digitally signed[/b], so Windows SmartScreen may show a warning. SHA-256 of [i]MO2-Revamped-Setup-1.0.1.exe[/i]:
[code]8AE75917426AF3CAA563A0D7B8AA149907CE3E950204B731BA5306DB4BB9CF48[/code]In PowerShell:
[code]Get-FileHash .\MO2-Revamped-Setup-1.0.1.exe[/code]
[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the main file and run [i]MO2-Revamped-Setup-1.0.1.exe[/i].[/*]
[*]Pick your language and choose [b]Install isolated Elden Ring[/b].[/*]
[*]Choose the installation folder. MO2 Revamped starts automatically when setup finishes, in the language you chose.[/*]
[*]Point it at your Elden Ring folder and follow the first-start prompts (profile, theme and categories).[/*]
[/list]
The isolated edition is a self-contained, portable MO2: profiles, mods, downloads and settings all live inside its own folder. It never reads or changes an existing Mod Organizer 2 installation, so both can be used side by side.

[b]Updating:[/b] run the new setup and choose [b]Update[/b]. Your data is kept and the previous files are backed up first.
[b]Uninstalling:[/b] run the setup and choose [b]Uninstall[/b]. The option to erase your data starts unchecked.
The Standard multi-instance installation and [i]Copy data[/i] are shown as [i]coming soon[/i].

[size=5][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[b]Elden Ring tools[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Archive installer[/b]: keep a mod's original folder layout or use MO2's standard layout; optionally omit .txt and .md files.[/*]
[*][b]Native DLL Profile[/b]: per-profile load order for native DLL mods, loaded through the Revamped native bridge.[/*]
[*][b]Startup Options[/b]: start minimized, black background (both now apply on every launch), [b]skip the intro logo screens[/b], and optional cleanup after the game closes.[/*]
[*][b]Save Isolation[/b] ([i]Tools > Save Isolation[/i]): separate saves per profile, shared saves within the installation, or the global Steam save, with named save profiles and safe copy actions.[/*]
[/list]
[b]Interface[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Six languages[/b]: English, Spanish, German, French, Italian and Brazilian Portuguese, across the interface, tutorials and every Revamped tool.[/*]
[*]Three themes: [b]Light[/b], [b]Dark Blue[/b] and [b]Dark Black[/b].[/*]
[*]Reworked main window, menus, file panes, log area, filters, category manager, Overwrite view and dialogs.[/*]
[*]Every dialog stays on screen, so buttons remain reachable on 768p displays and at 150% scaling.[/*]
[/list]
[b]Installer[/b]
[list]
[*]One setup file to install, update, restore and uninstall, in six languages.[/*]
[*]Integrity checks and backups before updates; only maintains folders it recognizes as MO2 Revamped.[/*]
[*]Starts MO2 without administrator rights after installing.[/*]
[/list]
[spoiler]
[b]Bundled runtime:[/b] Mod Organizer 2 2.5.2 · USVFS 0.5.7.2 · Qt/PyQt 6.7.1 · Python 3.12.15 · OpenSSL 3.5.9 · 7-Zip 24.05 · LOOT CLI 1.6.0 / libloot 0.23.0 · Explorer++ 1.4.0
[b]Native bridge:[/b] 0.5.0-alpha.35. The product version (1.0.1) does not mean each Elden Ring component has reached 1.0.
[b]Logo skip:[/b] if the game version is not recognized, the logos simply play as usual.[/spoiler]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.[/*]
[*]Elden Ring (Steam).[/*]
[*][url=https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vc_redist.x64.exe]Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 Redistributable (x64)[/url] (usually already installed).[/*]
[*]No other mods required.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b]Source code, license and bugs[/b][/size]
Free software under the [b]GNU General Public License v3[/b]. Source code and releases: [url=https://github.com/ArialSenki/MO2-Revamped]github.com/ArialSenki/MO2-Revamped[/url]
To report a bug, use the [b]Bugs[/b] tab and include your Windows version, the steps to reproduce it and the bug-report ZIP that MO2 Revamped can create (or [i]logs/mo_interface.log[/i]). Remove personal paths before posting, and never attach saves or account data.

